WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.060
Let T of X have integer coefficients
on a cycle of length two to the k,

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:09.893
with k at least one. Suppose T times
its star equals two to the power two t,

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.300
times w squared, where t is a
nonnegative integer and w is odd.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:18.780
We will prove that every opposite
coefficient difference is divisible by

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:22.220
two to the t. The coefficients
need not be signs.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:27.700
Choose a primitive root of
unity xi of order two to the k,

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.780
and let D be half that order.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:35.760
We now use a supplied cyclotomic input:
the specialization of Lemma two point one.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:40.920
After allowing rational numbers with
odd denominators, the first D powers,

00:00:41.587 --> 00:00:46.000
one, xi, through xi to the
D minus one, form a basis.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.240
In this ring,

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:52.540
powers of xi minus one measure
divisibility through a valuation v,

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.600
normalized by v of two equals one.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:00.820
This is an arithmetic measure, not
complex magnitude. The supplied fact is:

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:06.160
if the valuation of the sum of b
j times xi to the j is at least t,

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:11.260
and the b j are integers, then every
b j is divisible by two to the t.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:17.090
The basis comes from the cyclotomic
polynomial X to the D plus one.

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:22.650
Replacing X by one plus Y gives
an Eisenstein polynomial at two.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:29.500
Also, two is a unit times the D-th
power of xi minus one. These standard

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:33.680
properties are the input that lets us read
divisibility coefficient by coefficient.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:37.840
Now substitute X equal to xi.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.960
Star becomes complex conjugation,

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:47.480
so T of xi times its conjugate equals
two to the power two t, times w squared.

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:51.680
Apply the valuation:
multiplication becomes addition.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:58.547
The odd number w has valuation zero,
so the right side has valuation two t.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:02.460
The two factors on the
left have equal valuation.

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:09.620
Conjugation sends xi minus one to
negative xi inverse times xi minus one.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:13.360
That multiplier is a unit, so it
does not change the valuation.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:17.540
Therefore twice the valuation
of T of xi equals two t,

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:20.300
and the valuation of T of xi equals t.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:25.020
Finally use xi to the
D equals negative one.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:29.200
Pair a j times xi to the
j with the opposite term,

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:33.260
a sub j plus D times xi to the j plus D.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.110
Replace the extra xi to
the D by negative one.

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:41.000
Their sum becomes a j
minus a sub j plus D,

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:45.060
times xi to the j. Do this
for every opposite pair.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:51.920
Now T of xi is written in our basis, with
coefficients a j minus a sub j plus D.

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:55.960
Its valuation is t. The supplied
basis fact therefore makes

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:59.000
every one of these differences
divisible by two to the t.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:02.480
This proves our claim from
the stated cyclotomic input.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:07.950
For a hypothetical order sixteen
row, take k equal to four,

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:11.230
t equal to two, and w equal to one.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:16.393
Here the coefficients are signs. Their
possible differences are negative two,

00:03:16.827 --> 00:03:20.390
zero, or two. Only zero
is divisible by four,

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:24.120
so every entry equals the
entry eight positions away.

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:27.160
The eighth cyclic shift
would repeat the row.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:32.410
Its dot product with the original would
be sixteen, instead of the required zero.

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:36.110
This illustration excludes order sixteen.

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:40.200
In the general descent, the
coefficients may be larger odd integers.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.760
We keep the divisibility result,

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:46.480
which will let the folding step compare
and average opposite coefficients.
